  {
   "approach": "From the trailhead at the end of the long forest road out of the Slocan Valley (road condition varies from year to year), a well-graded trail climbs steeply through forest and then breaks out into open alpine. It leads to the camp area at the foot of the mountain, known as the Beach, which has an outhouse, and on to the toe of the South Ridge. The trail passes the South Ridge start, runs close under the West Face, then dips on its way toward the col between Gimli and Niselheim. Do not follow the downhill section; instead head up and left to the start, just left of the more obvious cracks of Lusting After Women.",
   "area_id": "bc_mount_gimli",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": null,
   "description": null,
   "discipline": "trad",
   "grade": "5.10d PG13",
   "id": "bc_mount_gimli_another_dimension",
   "name": "Another Dimension",
   "need_approach": false,
   "need_descent": true,
   "parent": "Valhalla Mountains",
   "peak": "Mount Gimli",
   "peak_elev": null,
   "peak_lat": 49.7655,
   "peak_lng": -117.6478,
   "pitches": 8
  },
  {
   "approach": "From the trailhead at the end of the long forest road out of the Slocan Valley (road condition varies from year to year), a well-graded trail climbs steeply through forest and then breaks out into open alpine. It leads to the camp area at the foot of the mountain, known as the Beach, which has an outhouse, and on to the toe of the South Ridge. Keep to the main trail beyond the Beach and the southwest face, heading for the col into Mulvey Basin. Once the trail has dropped steeply and started to rise again, watch for a shallow corner crack in dark rock on the west face; the first pitch starts at its base.",
   "area_id": "bc_mount_gimli",
